  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>The graph shows the cycle of a heat engine operating with an ideal monatomic gas. It consists of three stages: an isothermal A → B, an isobaric B → C and an adiabatic C → A. The temperature at A is 560 K.</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Show that the thermal energy transferred from the gas along B → C is about 700 J. [3]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> The work done along A → B is 840 J. Calculate the efficiency of the engine. [3]</p></section>"
